From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: default to LOGERROR|LOGINFO only

The radxa-pkg build enables every debug class (LOGTRACE/LOGDEBUG/LOGFW)
by default, which floods the kernel log and the serial console with
per-beacon and per-message traces (rwnx_rx_handle_msg spam during
scans).  Keep errors and the INFO identity lines (chipmatch, firmware
path, clock) that the test documentation relies on, drop the rest.
The fdrv level stays runtime-tunable via /sys/module/aic8800_fdrv/
parameters/aicwf_dbg_level if verbose tracing is ever needed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [default debug configuration]
---
--- a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@
 
 
 extern uint8_t scanning;
-int aicwf_dbg_level = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE|LOGFW;
+int aicwf_dbg_level = LOGERROR|LOGINFO;
 module_param(aicwf_dbg_level, int, 0660);
 #ifdef CONFIG_DYNAMIC_PWR
 int dynamic_pwr = 1;
--- a/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
+++ b/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
@@ -15,7 +15,8 @@
 #define DRV_AUTHOR            "AICSemi"
 #define DRV_VERS_MOD          "1.0"
 
-int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE;
+/* not registered as a module_param: quiet by default, no runtime knob */
+int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR|LOGINFO;
 
 struct semaphore aicbsp_probe_semaphore;
 
